# A damage floor's white field is the whole palette (build 157b). loc_7108
# (ps2.asm:10430) runs inside ObjCL_Main, the leader's object: it writes
# $EEE into all 64 entries and waits for a field there, puts the palette
# back from $FB80 and waits seven more, takes the HP, and only then
# returns -- the rest of LevelScreenLoop's iteration (the other objects,
# ProcessAButtonPress, ProcessRandomBattle, loc_6430's colour cycles) runs
# after the eight fields. Until 157b the port ran that rest in the white
# field's own tick, so on Gaira loc_6430 wrote its star entries over the
# white (the palette path showed line 3 entry 10 at $CAA), and the cycle
# step the ROM shows at the stall's end was put back by loc_7140 instead.
# Gaira, from the open cell above the floor: the second step, off 3,6.

start level $41 3 5
party 1 1
wait idle
walk down 2                  # off 3,6: the white field is this tick
shot 01_white
expect pixel 24 5 $EEE       # a star, line 3 entry 10, white with the rest
expect stat 0 hp 19          # loc_7162 comes after the fields
wait ticks 1
expect pixel 24 5 $000       # loc_7140: the palette as loaded
wait ticks 6
expect pixel 24 5 $000       # the seventh field
wait ticks 1
shot 02_rest
expect pixel 24 5 $CAA       # the iteration's rest: loc_6430's step
expect stat 0 hp 18
